# Ignore policy.
#
# Written after an audit found 14.8 MB of agent run artifacts sitting untracked inside this
# repository: 3,653 files, 1,919 directories, 27 nested `.git` repositories and 104 `__pycache__`
# directories, none of them referenced by any tracked file. It is not only untidiness. The repository
# states the opposite policy about itself in AGENTS.md and README.md ("exploration may branch, the
# repository must converge"), and the run that produced the archive declared its artifact root as
# `D:\AI-Runs\overnight-20260913\` — a path that does not exist. The only copy is inside this tree.
#
# This file is the structural fix: agent scratch can now never be staged by accident, and the
# accident cannot recur silently. It does NOT delete anything. The archive is kept in place because it
# is another run's primary evidence, and `git status` going quiet is not the same as the evidence
# being worthless.

# --- Agent run artifacts -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Untracked working area for autonomous runs. A run that needs to leave evidence should write a
# curated summary into reports/ or research/ and keep its raw sandboxes here.
/AI-Runs/

# A 0-byte file named `nul` — a Windows reserved device name — was created in the repository root by
# an agent's `>nul` redirect typo and survived for eleven days. Listed so the name is never staged
# even if a tool recreates it.
/nul

# --- Regenerable output --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled Python caches appeared 104 times inside the archive above and inside evaluation sandboxes.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# `npm pack` output and installed dependencies.
*.tgz
node_modules/

# --- Scratch conventions -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The paths PC-5 of the project-conventions skill points at. A scratch file belongs here or outside
# the repository — never loose in the tree.
/.scratch/
/tmp/
